{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrsXSVNd9yQJpsNB6Qk8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Bundles suite: each marker is found in its named control file, and the test output names that file.\n[x] Bundles suite: the render support marker is absent from the browser adapter entry, each chunk it imports, and its min build, with one assertion per file.\n[x] Bundles suite: the `preact-render-to-string` marker is absent from both browser adapter files.\n[x] Bundles suite: no non-adapter `dist` entry or its chunks imports `preact`, with one assertion per file.\n[x] A marker missing from its control file fails with a message saying the marker is stale (verified with a temporary bogus marker during development, not committed).\n[x] `npm run gate` runs the suite and passes.\n\nTicket 05 is done. A new suite, `test/bundles.ts`, run with `npm run test:bundles`, reads the built `dist/` and proves the browser adapter carries no render code and no other entry imports `preact`. It sits in `gate` right after `size`, and the full gate passes (exit 0, including `npm test` with 454 passing). Everything is in one commit, `dde7f55`.\n\n**How it works:** a `MARKERS` table pairs each fixed string with a control file and a list of files that must lack it. Each entry file is read together with every chunk it imports, following relative `import`/`from` specifiers in both the normal and minified output. For each marker, the suite first checks the control. If the string is missing there, it fails saying the marker is stale and names the files it searched. Otherwise it makes one assertion per checked file.\n\n**Marker choices:**\n1. **Render support:** `&#39;`, from the attribute escaper's table. Its code lives in a shared chunk (`chunk-RKWPTT6P.js`), not in `dist/render-support.js` itself, so that check only works because controls are read with their chunks too.\n2. **`preact-render-to-string`:** `dist/preact.js` does not import it (the caller does the rendering), so the control I picked is `node_modules/preact-render-to-string/package.json`. That file proves how the import name is spelled, but not that it survives bundling. This marker is the weakest of the three.\n3. **`preact`:** the quoted string `\"preact\"`, which matches both `from \"preact\"` and the minified `from\"preact\"`. The control is `dist/preact.js`, and the 11 entries the ticket lists are checked with their chunks.\n\n**Proof that the suite can fail:** it passed on its first run because the split already held, so I checked it with temporary changes, all reverted before the final gate run:\n- Importing render support in `src/preact.browser.ts` and rebuilding failed on the chunk and on the min file.\n- Adding a `preact-render-to-string` import to the min build, and a `preact` import to `dist/util.js`, each failed on exactly that file.\n- A made-up marker failed with the stale message.\n\n`npm pkg set` reordered `peerDependencies` in `package.json`, so I put that back as it was. AGENTS.md has a new paragraph on the suite and its table, and attempt notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` (not committed)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":170,"cache_read_input_tokens":76882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":170},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"198adc52-88a1-49ae-9ead-e11af037c9ee","uuid":"08533b6a-3332-422b-a415-ff08ed77fa09","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:21:42.566Z","request_id":"req_011CgrsXSFyUvGZCvBYwScC1"}
